Story: Flying with a TX15 on the serial line
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the sticks to reach the plane through the flight computer
  So that I fly the way I fly the real plane

  You connect the TX15 to the flight computer with a serial line. The sticks move the
  channels of the autopilot, and the screen of the TX15 shows what the plane does. You arm
  the plane, ArduPilot changes its mode, and the TX15 shows the new mode.

  Scenario: Fly and watch the screen
    Given the TX15 screen mode is AUTO
    And the TX15 screen arming is armed
    And the TX15 screen battery is 11.1 V
    And the TX15 screen bank is 30 degrees
    And the ground station telemetry is flowing
    And the ground station map distance is 400 m
    And the TX15 arm switch is on
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the arm channel is at least 1900 us
    And the TX15 screen mode is AUTO
    And the TX15 screen arming is armed
    And the TX15 screen battery is at least 11 V
    And the TX15 screen battery is at most 11.2 V
    And the TX15 screen bank is at least 29 degrees
    And the TX15 screen bank is at most 31 degrees
    And the ground station telemetry is flowing
    And the ground station map distance is at least 399 m
    And the ground station map distance is at most 401 m

  Scenario: Full travel on the sticks
    Given the TX15 roll stick is 100 %
    And the TX15 pitch stick is -50 %
    And the TX15 throttle stick is 100 %
    And the TX15 arm switch is on
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the roll channel is at least 1990 us
    And the pitch channel is at least 1245 us
    And the pitch channel is at most 1255 us
    And the throttle channel is at least 1990 us
    And the arm channel is at least 1900 us

  Scenario: Sticks centred
    Given the TX15 roll stick is 0 %
    And the TX15 pitch stick is 0 %
    And the TX15 throttle stick is 0 %
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the roll channel is 1500 us
    And the pitch channel is 1500 us

  Scenario: A damaged line
    Given the corrupted frames are 100 %
    And the TX15 roll stick is 100 %
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the roll channel is 1500 us

Story: Losing the TX15 and getting it back
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the plane to fail safe when the line goes quiet
  So that a lost link does not leave the throttle open

  You unplug the TX15 while the throttle is at half. The flight computer sets the throttle
  below the failsafe level of ArduPilot. You plug the TX15 in, and the plane flies again.

  Scenario: Unplug
    Given the TX15 throttle stick is 50 %
    When the TX15 is not connected
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the throttle channel is at most 900 us
    And the TX15 uplink quality is 0 %

  Scenario: Plug in again
    Given the TX15 is not connected
    And the TX15 throttle stick is 50 %
    When the TX15 is connected
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the throttle channel is at least 1490 us
    And the TX15 uplink quality is 100 %

Story: Commanding the plane from the ground station
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the ground station to command the plane through the TX15
  So that it needs no radio of its own

  The ground station sends a command. It goes up the serial line, and ArduPilot gets it.
  The TX15 shows the new mode.

  Scenario: Command through the line
    Given the TX15 screen mode is RTL
    And the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When the ground station command is sent
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the autopilot command is received
    And the TX15 screen mode is RTL

  Scenario: The line is narrow
    Given the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When 10 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry rate is at most 4000 bytes per second
